  "id": "classical-conditioning",
  "term": "classical conditioning",
  "definition": "Classical conditioning is a form of learning in which different stimuli are presented close together in time so that a response becomes linked to one of them, without the response being followed by reward or punishment. It is also called Pavlovian conditioning.",
